 Primitive Age

 Purpose

The Primitive Age is the transition between vanilla survival and industrialization.

The player begins working with basic industrial materials and primitive processing systems while preparing the infrastructure required for the Steam Age.

The Primitive Age introduces the foundations of industrial production without providing access to advanced power generation, large-scale automation, or higher-tier machinery.

The primary purpose of this age is to establish the first production chains that will eventually require Steam-powered machinery.

 Resources

The Primitive Age primarily uses:

Iron
Copper
Tin
Zinc
Coal
Redstone
Stone
Flint
Clay
Glass
Wood

Additional resources may be required for specific production chains.

Resources belonging to higher technological tiers may generate naturally in the world, but their industrial uses remain restricted until the appropriate progression stage.

Finding a resource does not automatically grant access to the technology required to process it.

 Tools

Vanilla tools remain the primary tools during the Primitive Age.

The Primitive Age does not introduce a separate industrial tool tier.

Primitive progression is primarily based on infrastructure and processing rather than increasingly powerful personal equipment.

Higher-tier industrial tools remain locked until their respective progression stages.

 Processing

The Primitive Age introduces the first industrial material-processing chains.

Processing should remain primarily manual or require limited mechanical assistance.

The player begins converting raw resources into the components required for early industrial infrastructure.

Processing should be deliberately inefficient compared to later technological tiers.

The purpose of this limitation is to create a natural demand for Steam-powered machinery.

 Machines

Only basic primitive processing and mechanical systems are available during this age.

Machines introduced during the Primitive Age must:

Provide basic material processing
Prepare components for Steam infrastructure
Remain significantly less capable than Steam machinery
Avoid providing large-scale industrial automation
Avoid replacing the need for Steam-powered systems

Electric machines and higher-tier industrial machinery remain unavailable.

 Automation

Automation is intentionally limited.

Small-scale mechanical or utility automation may be available, but the player should still perform a significant amount of processing manually.

Primitive automation should primarily demonstrate the concept of production chains rather than provide complete industrial infrastructure.

Large-scale automated factories are reserved for the Steam Age and later technological tiers.

 Requirements

The player must complete the Starting Point before entering the Primitive Age.

The player should have:

Established a stable vanilla base
Secured reliable food and basic resources
Progressed through vanilla survival
Obtained the resources necessary to begin primitive industrial production
Established the basic infrastructure required for primitive processing

The Primitive Age should represent a deliberate transition away from purely vanilla survival.

 Exit Condition

The Primitive Age ends when the player has established the infrastructure required to enter the Steam Age.

The player must:

Establish basic industrial material processing
Produce the components required for Steam infrastructure
Establish a reliable supply of the resources required for Steam
Complete the primitive production chain
Construct the infrastructure required to begin Steam-powered production

Completion of these requirements unlocks the Steam Age.

The Primitive Age must not provide enough automation or processing power to replace Steam technology.

Steam is the intended solution to the limitations created by the Primitive Age.
